  "notes": "Unconfirmed: no North Korean government source could be reached; this comes from South Korean Ministry of Unification pages. Twelve-year compulsory education (2012) covers ages 5 to 17: one kindergarten year (left out here), five years of 소학교, three of 초급중학교 and three of 고급중학교, so 소학교 starts at six. Grades are numbered within each school (소학교 1–5학년, 초급·고급중학교 1–3학년)."
